================================================================================
## Read table descriptions from the Unity Catalog tables API
================================================================================

Context:
Reliance's Data Sources showed no table descriptions. `get_table_comment()`
queried `<catalog>.information_schema.tables`, which the app's service
principal cannot read in their workspace; the broad except swallowed the error
and returned "" for every table. Their local workaround parsed the text of
`DESCRIBE TABLE EXTENDED`.

Changes:

1. src/back/core/databricks/uc/UnityCatalog.py
   `get_table_comment()` reads `comment` from `GET /api/2.1/unity-catalog/tables/{full_name}`, the API `list_tables_and_views()` already uses, which needs only USE CATALOG, USE SCHEMA and SELECT. Identifiers are still validated first, and errors still return "".
2. tests/units/core/test_unity_catalog.py
   Replaced the information_schema SQL tests. Every case runs with SQL access refused; the tests cover the returned comment, the request URL, a table without a comment, and an API refusal.

Modified files:
- src/back/core/databricks/uc/UnityCatalog.py
- tests/units/core/test_unity_catalog.py
- changelogs/v0.8.2/dermotsmyth-db_2026-10-21.log

Tests: `uv run --frozen pytest -q -m "not scenario"` → 5939 passed, 316 skipped, 9 deselected, 0 failed in 38.05s. Deselected: 6 by the `not scenario` marker and the 3 network-bound health tests listed on 2026-10-19. The two new behaviour tests failed on the old code (SQL refused → ""; tables API never called).

